>Play a valkyrie.

i agree; valkyries are generally the easiest class to play; you
start out with a decent weapon, and decent armor (the shield is only
worth 4 ac, but then add that to the stuff you pick up; you generally
don't find shields in the dungeon for quite a while).  

Other tips:
 keep your pet alive.  Perhaps, if you have a chance and are doing well
  for food, get another pet; having the help in a fight against a tribe
  of orcs or somesuch is a bonus.
 always quaff from fountains in the beginning of the game.  Often you
  will die, but sometimes you'll get a wish.  
 learn how to engrave to check out wands. (look at the spoilers,
  e-mail me if you can't find them).  
 never put on armor/rings/amulets or wield weapons until you know cursed
  or not.  (pets will not walk on cursed items if they can help it...)
 Learn to run away.

You'll still lose a lot.  Enjoy... 
